{
  "id": 312048803,
  "iid": 16214,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "MATE: Improve reporting of a mate config syntax error",
  "description": "Fix the mate lexer to increment the line count when consuming any\nto-the-end-of-line comment (\"//\"). Without this fix the user is\nincorrectly directed to look at an earlier line number in a mate\nconfig file than the actual source of the syntax error.\n\nUpdate the configuration_error() function defined in mate's grammer\nfile to better report the case when a syntax error is detected at\nthe end of file. Without this fix the %s parameter to the format\nstring may have a NULL yyminor value. Quote the text of the yyminor\nvalue printed in the format string.\n\nWhile here update the case for the text 'Syntax Error' and 'Parse\nError' to follow the more conventional use of a lower case 'e' for\nthe word \"error\".",
